/-!
# Coherent sheaves of modules form a weak Serre subcategory

On a ringed space, the coherent sheaves of modules form a weak Serre subcategory of the category of
all sheaves of modules: they contain the zero object, are closed under isomorphisms, and are closed
under kernels, cokernels and extensions.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.overOverEquivalence` is the equivalence, induced by
  `CategoryTheory.Over.iteratedSliceEquiv`, between sheaves of modules on the slice site at
  `Z.left` and sheaves of modules on the iterated slice site at `Z : Over U`, and
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.overOverIso` identifies `(M.over U).over Z` with `M.over Z.left` through
  it.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.localGeneratorsDataPushforward` is local generators data transported
  along the restriction of sheaves of modules induced by a continuous and cocontinuous functor of
  sites.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteType_pushforward`: being of finite type transports along the
  restriction of sheaves of modules induced by an equivalence of sites; with it,
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteType_of_overOverEquivalence_inverse` moves finite type between
  the slice site at `Z.left` and the iterated slice site at `Z`.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteType_over_of_isFiniteType`: restriction to an object of the site
  preserves being of finite type.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteType_X₂_of_shortExact`: the middle term of a short exact sequence
  whose first term is of finite type and whose third term is generated by finitely many global
  sections is of finite type, over an arbitrary site.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteType_kernel_of_isCoherent` and
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteType_kernel_over_of_isCoherent`: the kernel of a morphism from a
  sheaf of modules of finite type to a coherent one (respectively to the restriction of a coherent
  one to an open) is of finite type.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isCoherent_kernel`: the kernel of a morphism of coherent sheaves of
  modules is coherent.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isCoherent_X₃_of_shortExact`: the third term of a short exact sequence
  whose first two terms are coherent is coherent.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isCoherent_X₂_of_shortExact`: the middle term of a short exact sequence
  whose outer terms are coherent is coherent.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.coherentModules_isWeakSerreClass`: the coherent sheaves of modules form a
  weak Serre subcategory.

## Implementation notes

The space, the sheaf of rings, the sections and the index types of the free modules all live in one
universe `u`, as in the coherence predicate of
`StacksFrontier/Algebra/Category/ModuleCat/Sheaf/Coherent.lean`. The results about an arbitrary site
are stated for `C : Type u` with `Category.{u} C`, so that they apply both to `Opens X` and to its
slice categories `Over U`.

The condition `IsCoherent.kernel_isFiniteType` quantifies over the slice site at an open `U`.
Sheaves of modules on the slice site of a slice site are compared with sheaves of modules on the
slice site at `Z.left` through `overOverEquivalence`, which is why the instances
`HasSheafify (((J.over Y).over Z).over W) AddCommGrpCat.{u}` appear; for the site of opens of a
space they are available.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01BY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01BY)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01B7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01B7)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0754](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0754)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace SheafOfModules ZeroObject

universe u

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules

/-! ### An epimorphism induces an epimorphism of kernels -/

section Abelian

variable {A : Type*} [Category* A] [Abelian A]

/-- In an abelian category, if `p` is an epimorphism then the induced morphism
`kernel (p ≫ f) ⟶ kernel f` is an epimorphism. -/
lemma epi_kernelMap_of_epi {Y Z W : A} (p : Y ⟶ Z) [Epi p] (f : Z ⟶ W) :
    Epi (kernel.map (p ≫ f) f p (𝟙 _) (by simp)) := by
  let s := kernelCokernelCompSequence p f
  have hExact := (kernelCokernelCompSequence_exact p f).exact 1
  have hπ : cokernel.π p = 0 := IsZero.eq_of_tgt (isZero_cokernel_of_epi p) _ _
  have hDelta : s.map' 2 3 = 0 := by
    show kernelCokernelCompSequence.δ p f = 0
    rw [kernelCokernelCompSequence.δ_fac, hπ]
    simp only [CategoryTheory.Limits.comp_zero, neg_zero]
  have hExact' :
      (ShortComplex.mk (s.map' 1 2) (0 : s.obj' 2 ⟶ s.obj' 3) (by simp)).Exact := by
    change (ShortComplex.mk (s.map' 1 2) (s.map' 2 3) _).Exact at hExact
    simpa only [hDelta] using hExact
  have hEpi' : Epi (s.map' 1 2) :=
    ((CategoryTheory.Abelian.tfae_epi (s.map' 1 2) (s.obj' 3)).out 3 1).mp hExact'
  show Epi (kernel.map (p ≫ f) f p (𝟙 _) (by simp))
  convert hEpi' using 1 <;> rfl

/-- If `kernel.ι ψ` factors through a monomorphism `ι` then the kernel of `ι ≫ ψ` is the kernel
of `ψ`: pulling `ker ψ` back along a monomorphism it already lies in changes nothing. -/
noncomputable def kernelCompIsoOfFactorsThrough {K Y Z : A} (ι : K ⟶ Y) [Mono ι] (ψ : Y ⟶ Z)
    (l : kernel ψ ⟶ K) (hl : l ≫ ι = kernel.ι ψ) : kernel (ι ≫ ψ) ≅ kernel ψ :=
  have : Mono l := mono_of_mono_fac hl
  IsLimit.conePointUniqueUpToIso (kernelIsKernel (ι ≫ ψ))
    (KernelFork.IsLimit.ofι' (f := ι ≫ ψ) l
      (by rw [← Category.assoc, hl, kernel.condition])
      (fun {_} k hk => ⟨kernel.lift ψ (k ≫ ι) (by rw [Category.assoc]; exact hk),
        by rw [← cancel_mono ι, Category.assoc, hl, kernel.lift_ι]⟩))

/-- Pulling back a short exact sequence along a morphism into its quotient: if `a` is a kernel of
`g`, then its lift `l` into the pullback of `f` along `g` is a kernel of the first projection. -/
noncomputable def isLimitKernelForkPullbackFst {K W Y Z : A} (f : W ⟶ Z) (g : Y ⟶ Z)
    {a : K ⟶ Y} {ha : a ≫ g = 0} (hker : IsLimit (KernelFork.ofι a ha)) [Mono a]
    (l : K ⟶ pullback f g) (hl₁ : l ≫ pullback.fst f g = 0)
    (hl₂ : l ≫ pullback.snd f g = a) : IsLimit (KernelFork.ofι l hl₁) :=
  have : Mono l := mono_of_mono_fac hl₂
  KernelFork.IsLimit.ofι' _ _ fun {_} k hk =>
    ⟨(KernelFork.IsLimit.lift' hker (k ≫ pullback.snd f g)
        (by rw [Category.assoc, ← pullback.condition, ← Category.assoc, hk, zero_comp])).1, by
      refine pullback.hom_ext ?_ ?_
      · rw [Category.assoc, hl₁, comp_zero, hk]
      · rw [Category.assoc, hl₂]
        exact (KernelFork.IsLimit.lift' hker (k ≫ pullback.snd f g) _).2⟩

/-- The kernel of the second projection of the pullback of `f` along `g` is the kernel of `f`. -/
noncomputable def isLimitKernelForkPullbackSnd {K W Y Z : A} {f : W ⟶ Z} (g : Y ⟶ Z)
    {i : K ⟶ W} {hi : i ≫ f = 0} (hker : IsLimit (KernelFork.ofι i hi)) [Mono i]
    (j : K ⟶ pullback f g) (hj₁ : j ≫ pullback.fst f g = i)
    (hj₂ : j ≫ pullback.snd f g = 0) : IsLimit (KernelFork.ofι j hj₂) :=
  have : Mono j := mono_of_mono_fac hj₁
  KernelFork.IsLimit.ofι' _ _ fun {_} k hk =>
    ⟨(KernelFork.IsLimit.lift' hker (k ≫ pullback.fst f g)
        (by rw [Category.assoc, pullback.condition, ← Category.assoc, hk, zero_comp])).1, by
      refine pullback.hom_ext ?_ ?_
      · rw [Category.assoc, hj₁]
        exact (KernelFork.IsLimit.lift' hker (k ≫ pullback.fst f g) _).2
      · rw [Category.assoc, hj₂, comp_zero, hk]⟩

end Abelian

/-! ### Finite type kernels -/

section Site

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{u} C] [HasBinaryProducts C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}}
  [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ Y : C, HasSheafify (J.over Y) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ Y : C, (J.over Y).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]

/-- If the kernel of `p ≫ f` is of finite type and `p` is an epimorphism, then the kernel of
`f` is of finite type: it is the image of the former under the induced morphism. -/
theorem isFiniteType_kernel_of_epi_comp {M N P : SheafOfModules.{u} R} (p : M ⟶ N) [Epi p]
    (f : N ⟶ P) (h : (kernel (p ≫ f)).IsFiniteType) : (kernel f).IsFiniteType := by
  let km := kernel.map (p ≫ f) f p (𝟙 _) (by simp)
  have : Epi km := epi_kernelMap_of_epi p f
  exact isFiniteType_of_epi km h

/-- Restriction to an object of the site preserves kernels. -/
noncomputable def overKernelIso {M N : SheafOfModules.{u} R} (φ : M ⟶ N) (V : C) :
    (kernel φ).over V ≅ kernel (φ.over V) :=
  PreservesKernel.iso (overFunctor.{u} R V) φ

/-- A kernel fork restricts to a kernel fork: restriction to an object of the site is additive
and preserves kernels. -/
noncomputable def isLimitKernelForkOver {M N P : SheafOfModules.{u} R} {f : M ⟶ N} {g : N ⟶ P}
    {hfg : f ≫ g = 0} (hf : IsLimit (KernelFork.ofι f hfg)) (V : C) :
    IsLimit (KernelFork.ofι (f.over V)
      (show (f.over V) ≫ (g.over V) = 0 by
        rw [← Functor.map_comp, hfg, Functor.map_zero])) :=
  KernelFork.mapIsLimit _ hf (overFunctor.{u} R V)

end Site

/-! ### Transport of finite type along an equivalence of sites -/

section Transport

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{u} C] {D : Type u} [Category.{u} D]
  {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {K : GrothendieckTopology D}
  {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}} {S : Sheaf K RingCat.{u}}
  [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ Y : C, HasSheafify (J.over Y) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ Y : C, (J.over Y).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [HasSheafify K AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [K.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ Y : D, HasSheafify (K.over Y) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ Y : D, (K.over Y).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]

/-- Local generators of a sheaf of modules, pushed forward along a continuous and cocontinuous
functor of sites: the covering family is the family of all objects of the source site admitting
a morphism into a member of the original covering family, and the generators are the original
generators restricted along that morphism. -/
noncomputable def localGeneratorsDataPushforward
    (G : D ⥤ C) [G.IsContinuous K J] [G.IsCocontinuous K J]
    (φ : S ⟶ (G.sheafPushforwardContinuous RingCat.{u} K J).obj R)
    (η : (SheafOfModules.pushforward φ).obj (unit R) ≅ unit S)
    [∀ Y : D, (Over.post G (X := Y)).IsContinuous (K.over Y) (J.over _)]
    (h : ∀ (Y : D) (Z : C) (f : G.obj Y ⟶ Z),
      PreservesColimitsOfSize.{u, u} <|
      SheafOfModules.pushforward.{u} (R := R.over Z)
        (F := Over.post (X := Y) G ⋙ Over.map f)
        (((Over.forget Y).sheafPushforwardContinuous RingCat.{u} (K.over Y) K).map φ))
    {M : SheafOfModules.{u} R} (P : M.LocalGeneratorsData) :
    ((SheafOfModules.pushforward φ).obj M).LocalGeneratorsData where
  I := Σ (Y : D) (i : P.I), G.obj Y ⟶ P.X i
  X i := i.1
  coversTop Y := by
    refine K.superset_covering ?_ <| G.cover_lift K _ (P.coversTop (G.obj Y))
    intro Z g ⟨i, ⟨v⟩⟩
    exact ⟨⟨Z, i, v⟩, ⟨𝟙 _⟩⟩
  generators i := by
    letI overS : SheafOfModules.{u} S ⥤ SheafOfModules.{u} (S.over i.1) :=
      SheafOfModules.pushforward (𝟙 _)
    letI G' := Over.post (X := i.1) G ⋙ Over.map i.2.2
    letI ψ : S.over i.1 ⟶
        (G'.sheafPushforwardContinuous RingCat.{u} (K.over i.1) (J.over (P.X i.2.1))).obj
          (R.over (P.X i.2.1)) :=
      ((Over.forget i.1).sheafPushforwardContinuous RingCat.{u} (K.over i.1) K).map φ
    letI e : (SheafOfModules.pushforward ψ).obj (unit (R.over (P.X i.2.1))) ≅
        unit (S.over i.1) := overS.mapIso η
    haveI : PreservesColimitsOfSize.{u, u, _} (SheafOfModules.pushforward ψ) := h _ _ _
    exact (P.generators i.2.1).map (SheafOfModules.pushforward ψ) e.symm

omit [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [HasSheafify K AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [K.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}] in
/-- If the local generators data `P` is of finite type, so is its transport
`localGeneratorsDataPushforward G φ η h P` along `G`. -/
lemma localGeneratorsDataPushforward_isFiniteType
    (G : D ⥤ C) [G.IsContinuous K J] [G.IsCocontinuous K J]
    (φ : S ⟶ (G.sheafPushforwardContinuous RingCat.{u} K J).obj R)
    (η : (SheafOfModules.pushforward φ).obj (unit R) ≅ unit S)
    [∀ Y : D, (Over.post G (X := Y)).IsContinuous (K.over Y) (J.over _)]
    (h : ∀ (Y : D) (Z : C) (f : G.obj Y ⟶ Z),
      PreservesColimitsOfSize.{u, u} <|
      SheafOfModules.pushforward.{u} (R := R.over Z)
        (F := Over.post (X := Y) G ⋙ Over.map f)
        (((Over.forget Y).sheafPushforwardContinuous RingCat.{u} (K.over Y) K).map φ))
    {M : SheafOfModules.{u} R} (P : M.LocalGeneratorsData) [P.IsFiniteType] :
    (localGeneratorsDataPushforward G φ η h P).IsFiniteType where
  isFiniteType := by
    rintro ⟨Y, j, f⟩
    have : (P.generators j).IsFiniteType :=
      SheafOfModules.LocalGeneratorsData.IsFiniteType.isFiniteType j
    exact ⟨by change Finite (P.generators j).I; infer_instance⟩

omit [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [HasSheafify K AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [K.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}] in
/-- Being of finite type transports along the restriction of sheaves of modules induced by an
equivalence of sites. -/
theorem isFiniteType_pushforward [HasPullbacks C] [HasPullbacks D]
    (G : D ⥤ C) [G.IsContinuous K J] [G.IsCocontinuous K J] [G.IsLeftAdjoint] [G.IsEquivalence]
    (φ : S ⟶ (G.sheafPushforwardContinuous RingCat.{u} K J).obj R) [IsIso φ]
    (η : (SheafOfModules.pushforward φ).obj (unit R) ≅ unit S)
    {M : SheafOfModules.{u} R} [M.IsFiniteType] :
    ((SheafOfModules.pushforward φ).obj M).IsFiniteType := by
  classical
  have (Y : D) : (Over.post (X := Y) G).IsContinuous (K.over Y) (J.over _) :=
    (Functor.isContinuous_iff_coverPreserving).2
      ((CoverPreserving.of_isContinuous G K J).overPost Y)
  obtain ⟨P, hP⟩ := SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType.exists_localGeneratorsData M
  have h : ∀ (Y : D) (Z : C) (f : G.obj Y ⟶ Z),
      PreservesColimitsOfSize.{u, u} <|
      SheafOfModules.pushforward.{u} (R := R.over Z)
        (F := Over.post (X := Y) G ⋙ Over.map f)
        (((Over.forget Y).sheafPushforwardContinuous RingCat.{u} (K.over Y) K).map φ) := by
    intro Y Z f
    let G' := Over.post (X := Y) G ⋙ Over.map f
    have : G'.IsContinuous (K.over Y) (J.over Z) :=
      Functor.isContinuous_comp _ _ _ (J.over _) _
    have : G'.IsCocontinuous (K.over Y) (J.over Z) := isCocontinuous_comp _ _ _ (J.over _)
    let a : S.over Y ⟶
        (G'.sheafPushforwardContinuous RingCat.{u} (K.over Y) (J.over Z)).obj (R.over Z) :=
      ((Over.forget Y).sheafPushforwardContinuous RingCat.{u} (K.over Y) K).map φ
    have : IsIso a := by dsimp only [a]; apply Functor.map_isIso
    have : (Over.post (X := Y) G).IsLeftAdjoint := inferInstance
    have : (Over.map f).IsLeftAdjoint := inferInstance
    have : G'.IsLeftAdjoint := by dsimp [G']; infer_instance
    have : (SheafOfModules.pushforward a).IsLeftAdjoint :=
      SheafOfModules.isLeftAdjoint_pushforward_of_isIso a
    infer_instance
  have hQ : (localGeneratorsDataPushforward G φ η h P).IsFiniteType :=
    have : P.IsFiniteType := hP
    localGeneratorsDataPushforward_isFiniteType G φ η h P
  exact SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType.mk.{u, u, u}
    ⟨(localGeneratorsDataPushforward G φ η h P).shrink,
      ⟨fun i => hQ.isFiniteType i.2.choose⟩⟩

end Transport

/-! ### The iterated slice site -/

section IteratedSlice

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{u} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}}

/-- The equivalence between sheaves of modules on the slice site of `C` at `Z.left` and sheaves
of modules on the slice site of the slice site of `C` at `U` at `Z`, induced by
`Over.iteratedSliceEquiv`. -/
noncomputable def overOverEquivalence (U : C) (Z : Over U) :
    SheafOfModules.{u} (R.over Z.left) ≌ SheafOfModules.{u} ((R.over U).over Z) :=
  SheafOfModules.pushforwardPushforwardEquivalence (Over.iteratedSliceEquiv Z)
    (S := (R.over U).over Z) (R := R.over Z.left) (𝟙 _) (𝟙 _)
    (by ext : 2; exact R.1.map_id _) (by ext : 2; exact R.1.map_id _)

/-- Restricting `M` first to `U` and then to `Z` is restricting it to `Z.left`, read through
`overOverEquivalence`. -/
noncomputable def overOverIso (M : SheafOfModules.{u} R) (U : C) (Z : Over U) :
    (overOverEquivalence U Z (R := R)).inverse.obj ((M.over U).over Z) ≅ M.over Z.left :=
  (overOverEquivalence U Z).fullyFaithfulFunctor.preimageIso
    ((overOverEquivalence U Z).counitIso.app ((M.over U).over Z))

variable [HasFiniteWidePullbacks C]
  [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ Y : C, HasSheafify (J.over Y) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ Y : C, (J.over Y).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ (Y : C) (Z : Over Y), HasSheafify ((J.over Y).over Z) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ (Y : C) (Z : Over Y), ((J.over Y).over Z).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ (Y : C) (Z : Over Y) (W : Over Z),
    HasSheafify (((J.over Y).over Z).over W) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ (Y : C) (Z : Over Y) (W : Over Z),
    (((J.over Y).over Z).over W).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]

/-- The inverse of `overOverEquivalence U Z` preserves colimits. -/
noncomputable instance preservesColimitsOverOverEquivalenceInverse (U : C) (Z : Over U) :
    PreservesColimitsOfSize.{u, u} (overOverEquivalence U Z (R := R)).inverse :=
  Adjunction.isEquivalence_preservesColimits _

omit [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ Y : C, HasSheafify (J.over Y) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ Y : C, (J.over Y).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}] in
/-- Being of finite type transports from the slice site at `Z.left` to the iterated slice site
at `Z`. -/
theorem isFiniteType_of_overOverEquivalence_inverse (U : C) (Z : Over U)
    {N : SheafOfModules.{u} ((R.over U).over Z)}
    (h : ((overOverEquivalence U Z (R := R)).inverse.obj N).IsFiniteType) : N.IsFiniteType := by
  have := h
  have h2 : ((overOverEquivalence U Z (R := R)).functor.obj
      ((overOverEquivalence U Z (R := R)).inverse.obj N)).IsFiniteType :=
    isFiniteType_pushforward (G := (Over.iteratedSliceEquiv Z).functor) (𝟙 _) (Iso.refl _)
  have h3 : (((overOverEquivalence U Z (R := R)).inverse ⋙
      (overOverEquivalence U Z (R := R)).functor).obj N).IsFiniteType := h2
  exact isFiniteType_of_iso.{u} ((overOverEquivalence U Z (R := R)).counitIso.app N)

end IteratedSlice

/-! ### Restriction preserves finite type -/

section Restrict

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{u} C] [HasFiniteWidePullbacks C] [HasBinaryProducts C]
  {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}}
  [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ Y : C, HasSheafify (J.over Y) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ Y : C, (J.over Y).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ (Y : C) (Z : Over Y), HasSheafify ((J.over Y).over Z) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ (Y : C) (Z : Over Y), ((J.over Y).over Z).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ (Y : C) (Z : Over Y) (W : Over Z),
    HasSheafify (((J.over Y).over Z).over W) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ (Y : C) (Z : Over Y) (W : Over Z),
    (((J.over Y).over Z).over W).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]

/-- Finitely many generating sections of `M.over Z.left` are finitely many generating sections of
`(M.over U).over Z`, read through `overOverEquivalence`. -/
noncomputable def generatingSectionsOverOver (M : SheafOfModules.{u} R) (U : C) (Z : Over U)
    (ρ : (M.over Z.left).GeneratingSections) : ((M.over U).over Z).GeneratingSections :=
  ρ.map (overOverEquivalence U Z).functor (Iso.refl _)

/-- `generatingSectionsOverOver M U Z ρ` is indexed by a finite type when `ρ` is. -/
instance finite_generatingSectionsOverOver (M : SheafOfModules.{u} R) (U : C) (Z : Over U)
    (ρ : (M.over Z.left).GeneratingSections) [Finite ρ.I] :
    Finite (generatingSectionsOverOver M U Z ρ).I :=
  inferInstanceAs (Finite ρ.I)

omit [HasBinaryProducts C] [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ (Y : C) (Z : Over Y) (W : Over Z),
    HasSheafify (((J.over Y).over Z).over W) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ (Y : C) (Z : Over Y) (W : Over Z),
    (((J.over Y).over Z).over W).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}] in
/-- Restriction to an object of the site preserves being of finite type. -/
theorem isFiniteType_over_of_isFiniteType (U : C) {M : SheafOfModules.{u} R} [M.IsFiniteType] :
    (M.over U).IsFiniteType := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨σ, hσ⟩ := SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType.exists_localGeneratorsData M
  have hcover : (J.over U).CoversTop (Subtype.val :
      { Z : Over U // ∃ ρ : ((M.over U).over Z).GeneratingSections, Finite ρ.I } → Over U) := by
    intro Y
    refine (J.over U).superset_covering ?_
      ((Over.forget U).cover_lift (J.over U) J (σ.coversTop Y.left))
    intro Z g hg
    obtain ⟨i, ⟨h⟩⟩ := (Sieve.mem_ofObjects_iff _ ((Over.forget U).map g)).1 hg
    have hfin : Finite (σ.generators i).I := (hσ.isFiniteType i).finite
    refine (Sieve.mem_ofObjects_iff _ g).2 ⟨⟨Z, ?_⟩, ⟨𝟙 Z⟩⟩
    exact ⟨generatingSectionsOverOver M U Z
      (generatingSectionsOfEpi (restrictFreeHom h (σ.generators i).π)), inferInstance⟩
  exact ⟨⟨{ I := { Z : Over U // ∃ ρ : ((M.over U).over Z).GeneratingSections, Finite ρ.I }
            X := Subtype.val
            coversTop := hcover
            generators := fun i => i.2.choose }, ⟨fun i => ⟨i.2.choose_spec⟩⟩⟩⟩

omit [HasFiniteWidePullbacks C]
  [∀ (Y : C) (Z : Over Y), HasSheafify ((J.over Y).over Z) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ (Y : C) (Z : Over Y), ((J.over Y).over Z).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ (Y : C) (Z : Over Y) (W : Over Z),
    HasSheafify (((J.over Y).over Z).over W) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ (Y : C) (Z : Over Y) (W : Over Z),
    (((J.over Y).over Z).over W).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}] in
/-- Over an object `V` carrying finitely many generating sections of `S.X₁` together with lifts
of the generating sections of `S.X₃`, the middle term of a short exact sequence is generated by
finitely many sections. -/
lemma exists_generatingSections_X₂ {S : ShortComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} R)} (hS : S.ShortExact)
    (τ : S.X₃.GeneratingSections) [Finite τ.I] (V : C) {A : Type u} [Finite A]
    (p : free A ⟶ S.X₁.over V) [Epi p]
    (υ : τ.I → (unit (R.over V) ⟶ S.X₂.over V))
    (hυ : ∀ k, υ k ≫ S.g.over V =
      (show unit (R.over V) ⟶ S.X₃.over V from (ιFree k ≫ τ.π).over V)) :
    ∃ ρ : (S.X₂.over V).GeneratingSections, Finite ρ.I := by
  have hb : FiniteTypeKernel.betaOf (R := R) V υ ≫ S.g.over V =
      (mapFreeIso (overFunctor R V) τ.I (FiniteTypeKernel.unitOverIso V)).hom ≫ (τ.π).over V :=
    FiniteTypeKernel.betaOf_spec S.g V τ.π υ hυ
  have : Epi ((τ.π).over V) := over_epi _ V
  have : Epi (FiniteTypeKernel.betaOf (R := R) V υ ≫ S.g.over V) := by
    rw [hb]; infer_instance
  have : Epi (freeSumHom (p ≫ S.f.over V) (FiniteTypeKernel.betaOf (R := R) V υ)) :=
    epi_freeSumHom (isColimitCokernelCoforkOver hS.gIsCokernel V) p _
  exact ⟨generatingSectionsOfEpi
    (freeSumHom (p ≫ S.f.over V) (FiniteTypeKernel.betaOf (R := R) V υ)),
    inferInstanceAs (Finite (A ⊕ τ.I))⟩

omit [∀ (Y : C) (Z : Over Y), HasSheafify ((J.over Y).over Z) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ (Y : C) (Z : Over Y), ((J.over Y).over Z).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ (Y : C) (Z : Over Y) (W : Over Z),
    HasSheafify (((J.over Y).over Z).over W) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ (Y : C) (Z : Over Y) (W : Over Z),
    (((J.over Y).over Z).over W).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}] in
/-- The middle term of a short exact sequence whose first term is of finite type and whose third
term is generated by finitely many global sections is of finite type. -/
theorem isFiniteType_X₂_of_shortExact {S : ShortComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} R)}
    (hS : S.ShortExact) [S.X₁.IsFiniteType] (τ : S.X₃.GeneratingSections) [Finite τ.I] :
    S.X₂.IsFiniteType := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨σ, hσ⟩ := SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType.exists_localGeneratorsData S.X₁
  have hepi : Epi S.g := hS.epi_g
  have hcover : J.CoversTop (Subtype.val :
      { V : C // ∃ ρ : (S.X₂.over V).GeneratingSections, Finite ρ.I } → C) := by
    intro Y
    choose T hT hlift using fun k : τ.I =>
      FiniteTypeKernel.exists_lift_over_of_epi S.g (ιFree k ≫ τ.π) Y
    refine J.superset_covering ?_ (J.intersection_covering
      (FiniteTypeKernel.iInf_mem J _ hT) (σ.coversTop Y))
    intro V g hg
    obtain ⟨hg₁, hg₂⟩ := hg
    rw [FiniteTypeKernel.iInf_apply] at hg₁
    obtain ⟨i, ⟨h⟩⟩ := (Sieve.mem_ofObjects_iff _ g).1 hg₂
    choose υ hυ using fun k => hlift k g (hg₁ k)
    have hfin : Finite (σ.generators i).I := (hσ.isFiniteType i).finite
    exact (Sieve.mem_ofObjects_iff _ g).2
      ⟨⟨V, exists_generatingSections_X₂ hS τ V (restrictFreeHom h (σ.generators i).π) υ hυ⟩,
        ⟨𝟙 V⟩⟩
  exact ⟨⟨{ I := { V : C // ∃ ρ : (S.X₂.over V).GeneratingSections, Finite ρ.I }
            X := Subtype.val
            coversTop := hcover
            generators := fun i => i.2.choose }, ⟨fun i => ⟨i.2.choose_spec⟩⟩⟩⟩

omit [∀ (Y : C) (Z : Over Y), HasSheafify ((J.over Y).over Z) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ (Y : C) (Z : Over Y), ((J.over Y).over Z).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ (Y : C) (Z : Over Y) (W : Over Z),
    HasSheafify (((J.over Y).over Z).over W) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ (Y : C) (Z : Over Y) (W : Over Z),
    (((J.over Y).over Z).over W).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}] in
/-- The pullback of a short exact sequence along a morphism out of a finite free sheaf of modules
is of finite type as soon as the sub-object is: it is an extension of the finite free sheaf by
that sub-object. -/
theorem isFiniteType_pullback_of_shortExact {S : ShortComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} R)}
    (hS : S.ShortExact) [S.X₁.IsFiniteType] {I : Type u} [Finite I] (ψ : free I ⟶ S.X₃) :
    (pullback ψ S.g).IsFiniteType := by
  have hepi : Epi S.g := hS.epi_g
  have hmono : Mono S.f := hS.mono_f
  have hw : (0 : S.X₁ ⟶ free I) ≫ ψ = S.f ≫ S.g := by rw [zero_comp, S.zero]
  have hzero : pullback.lift (0 : S.X₁ ⟶ free I) S.f hw ≫ pullback.fst ψ S.g = 0 :=
    pullback.lift_fst _ _ _
  have hT : (ShortComplex.mk (pullback.lift (0 : S.X₁ ⟶ free I) S.f hw)
      (pullback.fst ψ S.g) hzero).ShortExact :=
    { exact := ShortComplex.exact_of_f_is_kernel _
        (isLimitKernelForkPullbackFst ψ S.g hS.fIsKernel _ hzero (pullback.lift_snd _ _ _))
      mono_f := mono_of_mono_fac (pullback.lift_snd (0 : S.X₁ ⟶ free I) S.f hw)
      epi_g := inferInstance }
  have : Finite (free.generatingSections (R := R) I).I := inferInstanceAs (Finite I)
  exact isFiniteType_X₂_of_shortExact hT (free.generatingSections I)

end Restrict

section RingedSpace

variable {X : Type u} [TopologicalSpace X]
  {R : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) RingCat.{u}}

/-- Restriction to an open preserves short exact sequences. -/
private theorem shortExact_over {S : ShortComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} R)} (hS : S.ShortExact)
    (U : Opens X) : (ShortComplex.mk (S.f.over U) (S.g.over U)
      (by rw [← Functor.map_comp, S.zero, Functor.map_zero])).ShortExact :=
  have := hS.mono_f
  have := hS.epi_g
  { exact := ShortComplex.exact_of_f_is_kernel _ (isLimitKernelForkOver (hfg := S.zero)
      hS.fIsKernel U)
    mono_f := over_mono S.f U
    epi_g := over_epi S.g U }

/-- The kernel of a morphism from a sheaf of modules of finite type to a coherent sheaf of modules
is of finite type. -/
@[stacks 01BY "(2)"]
theorem isFiniteType_kernel_of_isCoherent {M N : SheafOfModules.{u} R} [M.IsFiniteType]
    [IsCoherent N] (φ : M ⟶ N) : (kernel φ).IsFiniteType := by
  obtain ⟨σ, hσ⟩ := SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType.exists_localGeneratorsData M
  have hloc : ∀ i, ((kernel φ).over (σ.X i)).IsFiniteType := fun i => by
    have hfin : Finite (σ.generators i).I := (hσ.isFiniteType i).finite
    have h1 : (kernel ((σ.generators i).π ≫ φ.over (σ.X i))).IsFiniteType :=
      IsCoherent.kernel_isFiniteType (σ.X i) (σ.generators i).I hfin _
    have h2 : (kernel (φ.over (σ.X i))).IsFiniteType :=
      isFiniteType_kernel_of_epi_comp (σ.generators i).π (φ.over (σ.X i)) h1
    exact isFiniteType_of_iso.{u} (M := kernel (φ.over (σ.X i)))
      (N := (kernel φ).over (σ.X i)) (overKernelIso φ (σ.X i)).symm
  have := hloc
  exact isFiniteType_of_coversTop (kernel φ) σ.X σ.coversTop

/-- The kernel of a morphism `g : N ⟶ M.over W` from a sheaf of modules generated by finitely many
sections to the restriction to `W` of a coherent sheaf of modules is of finite type. -/
theorem isFiniteType_kernel_of_generatingSections {M : SheafOfModules.{u} R} [IsCoherent M]
    (W : Opens X) {N : SheafOfModules.{u} (R.over W)} (σ : N.GeneratingSections) [Finite σ.I]
    (g : N ⟶ M.over W) : (kernel g).IsFiniteType :=
  isFiniteType_kernel_of_epi_comp σ.π g
    (IsCoherent.kernel_isFiniteType W σ.I inferInstance (σ.π ≫ g))

/-- The kernel of a morphism `f : K ⟶ M.over U` into the restriction of a coherent sheaf of modules
is of finite type over an object `Z` of the slice site over which `K` is generated by finitely many
sections. -/
theorem isFiniteType_kernel_over_aux {M : SheafOfModules.{u} R} [IsCoherent M]
    (U : Opens X) {K : SheafOfModules.{u} (R.over U)} (f : K ⟶ M.over U) (Z : Over U)
    (σ : (K.over Z).GeneratingSections) [Finite σ.I] :
    ((kernel f).over Z).IsFiniteType := by
  have key : (kernel (f.over Z)).IsFiniteType := by
    let e := overOverEquivalence (R := R) U Z
    have h3 : (kernel (e.inverse.map (f.over Z))).IsFiniteType := by
      have hfin : Finite (σ.map e.inverse (Iso.refl (unit (R.over Z.left)))).I :=
        inferInstanceAs (Finite σ.I)
      have h2 := isFiniteType_kernel_of_generatingSections Z.left
        (σ.map e.inverse (Iso.refl (unit (R.over Z.left))))
        (e.inverse.map (f.over Z) ≫ (overOverIso M U Z).hom)
      exact isFiniteType_of_iso.{u}
        (M := kernel (e.inverse.map (f.over Z) ≫ (overOverIso M U Z).hom))
        (N := kernel (e.inverse.map (f.over Z)))
        (kernel.mapIso _ (e.inverse.map (f.over Z))
          (Iso.refl _) (overOverIso M U Z).symm (by simp))
    have h4 : (e.inverse.obj (kernel (f.over Z))).IsFiniteType :=
      isFiniteType_of_iso.{u} (PreservesKernel.iso e.inverse (f.over Z)).symm
    exact isFiniteType_of_overOverEquivalence_inverse U Z h4
  exact isFiniteType_of_iso.{u} (overKernelIso f Z).symm

/-- The kernel of a morphism from a sheaf of modules of finite type on the slice site over an open
`U` to the restriction to `U` of a coherent sheaf of modules is of finite type. -/
theorem isFiniteType_kernel_over_of_isCoherent {M : SheafOfModules.{u} R} [IsCoherent M]
    (U : Opens X) {K : SheafOfModules.{u} (R.over U)} [K.IsFiniteType] (f : K ⟶ M.over U) :
    (kernel f).IsFiniteType := by
  obtain ⟨σ, hσ⟩ := SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType.exists_localGeneratorsData K
  have hloc : ∀ i, ((kernel f).over (σ.X i)).IsFiniteType := fun i =>
    have : Finite (σ.generators i).I := (hσ.isFiniteType i).finite
    isFiniteType_kernel_over_aux U f (σ.X i) (σ.generators i)
  have := hloc
  exact isFiniteType_of_coversTop (kernel f) σ.X σ.coversTop

/-- The kernel of a morphism of coherent sheaves of modules is coherent. -/
@[stacks 01BY "(3), kernels"]
theorem isCoherent_kernel {M N : SheafOfModules.{u} R} [IsCoherent M] [IsCoherent N]
    (φ : M ⟶ N) : IsCoherent (kernel φ) :=
  have : (kernel φ).IsFiniteType := isFiniteType_kernel_of_isCoherent φ
  isCoherent_of_mono (kernel.ι φ)

/-- The middle term of a short exact sequence of sheaves of modules whose outer terms are coherent
is coherent. -/
@[stacks 01BY "(4)", ega "0 5.3.3" "Extension clause"]
theorem isCoherent_X₂_of_shortExact {S : ShortComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} R)} (hS : S.ShortExact)
    (h₁ : IsCoherent S.X₁) (h₃ : IsCoherent S.X₃) : IsCoherent S.X₂ := by
  have := h₁
  have := h₃
  have := hS.mono_f
  refine { isFiniteType := ?_, kernel_isFiniteType := ?_ }
  · exact isFiniteType_middle_of_shortExact S hS IsCoherent.isFiniteType IsCoherent.isFiniteType
  intro U I hI φ
  have hmono : Mono (S.f.over U) := over_mono S.f U
  let e : kernel (S.g.over U) ≅ S.X₁.over U :=
    IsLimit.conePointUniqueUpToIso (kernelIsKernel (S.g.over U)) (shortExact_over hS U).fIsKernel
  have he : e.hom ≫ S.f.over U = kernel.ι (S.g.over U) :=
    IsLimit.conePointUniqueUpToIso_hom_comp (kernelIsKernel (S.g.over U))
      (shortExact_over hS U).fIsKernel WalkingParallelPair.zero
  have hq : (kernel (φ ≫ S.g.over U)).IsFiniteType :=
    IsCoherent.kernel_isFiniteType U I hI (φ ≫ S.g.over U)
  let δ : kernel (φ ≫ S.g.over U) ⟶ S.X₁.over U :=
    kernel.map (φ ≫ S.g.over U) (S.g.over U) φ (𝟙 _) (by simp) ≫ e.hom
  have hδ : δ ≫ S.f.over U = kernel.ι (φ ≫ S.g.over U) ≫ φ := by
    rw [show δ = kernel.map (φ ≫ S.g.over U) (S.g.over U) φ (𝟙 _) (by simp) ≫ e.hom from rfl,
      Category.assoc, he]
    exact kernel.lift_ι _ _ _
  have hδft : (kernel δ).IsFiniteType := isFiniteType_kernel_over_of_isCoherent U δ
  refine isFiniteType_of_iso.{u} (M := kernel δ) (N := kernel φ)
    ((kernelCompMono δ (S.f.over U)).symm ≪≫ kernelIsoOfEq hδ ≪≫
      kernelCompIsoOfFactorsThrough (kernel.ι (φ ≫ S.g.over U)) φ
        (kernel.lift (φ ≫ S.g.over U) (kernel.ι φ) (by rw [← Category.assoc]; simp))
        (kernel.lift_ι _ _ _))

/-- The third term of a short exact sequence of sheaves of modules whose first two terms are
coherent is coherent. -/
@[stacks 01BY "(3), cokernels", ega "0 5.3.3" "Quotient clause"]
theorem isCoherent_X₃_of_shortExact {S : ShortComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} R)} (hS : S.ShortExact)
    (h₁ : IsCoherent S.X₁) (h₂ : IsCoherent S.X₂) : IsCoherent S.X₃ := by
  have := h₁
  have := h₂
  have hepi : Epi S.g := hS.epi_g
  have hmonof : Mono S.f := hS.mono_f
  constructor
  · exact isFiniteType_of_epi.{u, u, u} (M := S.X₂) (N := S.X₃) S.g
      (IsCoherent.isFiniteType (M := S.X₂))
  intro U I hI ψ
  have hT := shortExact_over hS U
  have hX₁ : (S.X₁.over U).IsFiniteType := isFiniteType_over_of_isFiniteType U
  have hQ : (pullback ψ (S.g.over U)).IsFiniteType :=
    isFiniteType_pullback_of_shortExact hT ψ
  have hj : pullback.lift (kernel.ι ψ) (0 : kernel ψ ⟶ S.X₂.over U) (by simp) ≫
      pullback.snd ψ (S.g.over U) = 0 := pullback.lift_snd _ _ _
  have hker : (kernel (pullback.snd ψ (S.g.over U))).IsFiniteType :=
    isFiniteType_kernel_over_of_isCoherent U (pullback.snd ψ (S.g.over U))
  exact isFiniteType_of_iso.{u} (M := kernel (pullback.snd ψ (S.g.over U))) (N := kernel ψ)
    (IsLimit.conePointUniqueUpToIso (kernelIsKernel (pullback.snd ψ (S.g.over U)))
      (isLimitKernelForkPullbackSnd (S.g.over U) (hi := kernel.condition ψ) (kernelIsKernel ψ) _
        (pullback.lift_fst _ _ _) hj))

/-- The coherent sheaves of modules are closed under cokernels. -/
instance coherentModules_isClosedUnderCokernels :
    (coherentModules R).IsClosedUnderCokernels where
  cokernels_le := by
    rintro _ ⟨φ, k, hk, hφ⟩
    have h₁ : IsCoherent _ := hφ.1
    have h₂ : IsCoherent _ := hφ.2
    have hft : (Abelian.image φ).IsFiniteType :=
      isFiniteType_of_epi.{u, u, u} (N := Abelian.image φ) (Abelian.factorThruImage φ)
        IsCoherent.isFiniteType
    have himg : IsCoherent (Abelian.image φ) := isCoherent_of_mono (Abelian.image.ι φ)
    have hse : (ShortComplex.kernelSequence (cokernel.π φ)).ShortExact :=
      { exact := ShortComplex.kernelSequence_exact _
        mono_f := inferInstance
        epi_g := inferInstanceAs (Epi (cokernel.π φ)) }
    refine (coherentModules R).prop_of_iso
      (IsColimit.coconePointUniqueUpToIso (cokernelIsCokernel φ) hk) ?_
    exact isCoherent_X₃_of_shortExact hse himg h₂

/-- The coherent sheaves of modules are closed under extensions. -/
instance coherentModules_isClosedUnderExtensions :
    (coherentModules R).IsClosedUnderExtensions where
  prop_X₂_of_shortExact hS h₁ h₃ := isCoherent_X₂_of_shortExact hS h₁ h₃

/-- The coherent sheaves of modules are closed under kernels. -/
instance coherentModules_isClosedUnderKernels :
    (coherentModules R).IsClosedUnderKernels where
  kernels_le := by
    rintro _ ⟨φ, k, hk, hφ⟩
    have h₁ : IsCoherent _ := hφ.1
    have h₂ : IsCoherent _ := hφ.2
    exact (coherentModules R).prop_of_iso
      (IsLimit.conePointUniqueUpToIso (kernelIsKernel φ) hk) (isCoherent_kernel φ)

/-- On a ringed space, the coherent sheaves of modules form a weak Serre subcategory of the
category of all sheaves of modules: they contain the zero object, are closed under isomorphisms,
and are closed under kernels, cokernels and extensions. -/
@[stacks 01BY "coherent_weak_serre"]
instance coherentModules_isWeakSerreClass :
    ObjectProperty.IsWeakSerreClass (fun M : SheafOfModules.{u} R => IsCoherent M) where

end RingedSpace

end Stacks.SheafOfModules

